Task: Tests de escribir un Pattern suelto en un hueco (Fase 1, pattern-copy_20260910)

Red phase. Five cases for `Project.replacing(_ pattern: Pattern, at:)`: a loose
Pattern lands in the named slot of the selected Bank, every other slot and Bank
is left alone, existing material is replaced without mixing, out of range
returns the Project unchanged (FR24), and neither the selection nor the session
settings move.

Files: Packages/Engine/Tests/EngineTests/PatternCopyWithOriginTests.swift

Why: pasting across Banks needs an origin that is a value, not an index — the
clipboard holds the Pattern itself, and slot 3 of another Bank contains
something else entirely. `copyingSelectedPattern(to:)` cannot express that
(FR22). The name is an overload of the existing `replacing(_:at:)` rather than a
new verb, because `Bank` already writes a Pattern into a slot under that name
and the quality gate asks for no new synonyms.
